3.	(a) Two applicants who applied in June 1967 and one who applied in September 1967 have received final approval, (b) The three applicants mentioned in (a) above are currently living in their home.
4.	(a) Some discontent has been expressed by applicants over delay in acquiring a home. However, the difficulty being experienced is convincing the applicant that it is his responsibility to locate the house he wishes to purchase, or the type of house and area where he wishes to have a house constructed, (b) Six applicants have withdrawn their applications, generally for the following reasons: (i) unable to find a house within the approved amount of their application as related to income, and unable to finance the additional cost; or (ii) have changed their minds about buying a house, and have made other plans.

October 7, 1968
